Statistics as Numerical Set of Data (Plural Sense)
Statistics are collected for a pre-determined purpose - The purpose
of collecting statistical data must be decided in advance, otherwise
usefulness of the data collected would be negligible. Data collected
in an unsystematic manner and without complete awareness of the
purpose will be confusing and cannot be made on the basis of valid
conclusions.
Statistics are collected in a Systematic Manner - For accuracy or
reliability of data, the figures should be collected in a systematic
manner. If the figures are collected in a haphazard manner, the
reliability of such data will deteriorate. So, before collecting data,
suitable plan for their collection should be prepared.
